  "content": {
    "id": "p15-q4-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "6",
    "prompt": "Let $f(x)=\\dfrac{x}{x+1}$. Find $f(f(x))$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac{x}{2x+1}$, with $x\\ne-1,-\\dfrac12$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f(f(x))&=\\frac{\\frac{x}{x+1}}{\\frac{x}{x+1}+1}\\\\f(f(x))&=\\frac{\\frac{x}{x+1}}{\\frac{2x+1}{x+1}}\\\\f(f(x))&=\\frac{x}{x+1}\\cdot\\frac{x+1}{2x+1}\\\\f(f(x))&=\\frac{x}{2x+1}\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe original inner function requires $x\\ne-1$. The outer denominator also requires $2x+1\\ne0$, so $x\\ne-\\frac12$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 25
  },
